Statement of Purpose

The laws of most jurisdictions throughout the world automatically confer
exclusive Copyright and Related Rights (defined below) to the creator and/or
subsequent owner(s) of an original work of authorship and/or a database
(each, a "Work").

Certain owners wish to permanently relinquish those rights to a Work for the
purpose of contributing to a commons of creative, cultural and scientific
works ("Commons") that the public can reliably and without fear of later
claims of infringement build upon, modify, incorporate in other works,
reuse and redistribute as freely as possible in any form whatsoever and for
any purposes, including without limitation commercial purposes. These owners
may contribute to the Commons to promote the ideal of a free culture and the
further sharing of ideas and knowledge, and in sole reliance on the
foregoing reasons and without consideration of any kind or condition.

Affirmation of Dedication

The individual or entity dedicating the Work (the "Affirmer") hereby publicly,
permanently, knowingly, and irreversibly waives and relinquishes all of their
Copyright and Related Rights (defined below) in the Work to the maximum extent
permitted by applicable law.

This dedication includes, but is not limited to, the metadata matrix records, High-density token associations, and architectural lexicons contained herein.
